1
00:00:00,070 --> 00:00:02,250
The McDonald's ice cream machine isn't broken.

2
00:00:02,300 --> 00:00:03,090
It's locked.

3
00:00:03,140 --> 00:00:06,810
Every night it runs a four-hour heat cycle up to 151 degrees.

4
00:00:06,860 --> 00:00:09,720
If that cycle fails, it locks until a tech comes.

5
00:00:09,770 --> 00:00:12,300
Franchisees lose a lot of money every day it's down.

6
00:00:12,350 --> 00:00:16,630
Only Taylor techs can unlock it, for over $300 per fifteen minutes.

7
00:00:16,680 --> 00:00:19,970
So startup Kytch built a device that shows what's wrong on your phone.

8
00:00:20,020 --> 00:00:22,960
McDonald's told owners to remove it, citing safety risks.

9
00:00:23,010 --> 00:00:26,630
Kytch says that's false, and sued for $900 million.

10
00:00:26,680 --> 00:00:28,680
McDonald's calls the claims meritless.

11
00:00:28,730 --> 00:00:31,190
So next time it says broken… it might just be locked.
